# GNU Global C/C++ .vscode Config Pack

46 ready .vscode snippets and 21 audit rules across 8 setups: GNU Global gtags indexing, c_cpp_properties IntelliSense, gist workspaces, formatter save-actions, Dark+ colour overrides, Tailwind CSS, ASP.NET Core launch profiles, MicroProfile Java. VS Code never checks the values in these files — a defaultFormatter pointing at an extension id you never installed loads without a word and simply never formats.

## What it does for free

- All 21 rules run on the config file you have open, with no key and no limit
- All 46 snippets, across all 8 setups, inserted at the cursor
- The full contents printed by name, so you can check the pack before you rely on it

## With a licence

- **Audit the whole repository** — Opens every file in the workspace and runs the same check on each.
- **Rewrite the flagged lines** — Replaces the offending lines in the editor with the suggested text.
- **Write the findings to a file** — Asks CSV, JSON or HTML, then writes that file into the workspace folder.
- **Your team's own rules** — Opens Settings so you add your own rules; the free version is the built-in set.

## Install

```
ext install gnu-global-cpp-vscode-config-pack
```
